<%# Development only (`PublicPageRendering#note_stale_stylesheet`): the public
    stylesheet was not built for the theme in use, or the theme or the default
    styles changed after it was built. The CMS's own notice, outside the
    theme's frame, and no theme replaces it. In the flow, not fixed, so it
    moves nothing it does not have to. The command carries the THEME_PATH of
    the theme in use: without it the build makes the default theme's. %>
<% folder = ThemeFolder.current %>
<p role="status" class="border-b border-line bg-sunken px-4 py-2 text-center text-sm text-ink" data-stale-stylesheet>
  The public stylesheet is not up to date. Run <code><%= "THEME_PATH=#{Shellwords.escape(folder.path.to_s)} " if folder.configured? %>bin/rails tailwindcss:build</code> to rebuild it.
</p>
